sevillad@gmail.com wrote:
> [...]  I've read the spoilers, I'd like to know if I'd be doing
> something stupid by diluting any of these potions (maybe some of them
> are important):

Depends on how far you plan to reach in the game.

> blindness, booze, fruit, healing, gain energy, hallu, invisibility,
> levitation (I expect a ring someday), monster&object detection, oil,
> paralysis, restore ability, see invisible, sickness, sleeping, speed
> (I expect boots).

Any means to confuse yourself is helpful, so keep one or two booze or
resp. confusion (if you don't have other means to confuse yourself).

Potions of healing are good _if_ you managed to obtain a stack of them,
then you can alchemize for extra healing and finally full healing.

Gain energy is helpful if you are a spellcaster (and can help in some
alchemy recipes.

Invisibility might save your butt in emergencies, as long as you don't
already have it as intrinsic. But usually I dilute those potions from
the mid game on, often even earlier if I'm in dire needs of water.

I lately keep blessed levitation for the ascension run (you might not
yet be aiming at that; I just mention it) to have both ring slots free
while on the plane of air (where free action and some other helpful
ring is of good use).

A few blessed monster detection helps while in the Sanctum, but they
are especially good at Astral. Dilute them in early game

Paralysis is good against your quest nemesis.

Speed is good for alchemy of extra healing. Occasionally in emergencies.

> These I'd keep:
> 
> - FHeal,XHeal: i'd use them for MAX HP.
> - Conf: I've read that sometimes it's good to be confused to read/
> drink certain things.
> - Enligh: Blessed are good to raise stats.
> - Gain ability, gain level.
> - Polymorph: may not be useful, but looks so unpredictable it must be
> fun! (maybe a YASD will convince me soon...)

Some of the usages I mentioned might not be of interest on your current
level, but my first choices for the _early game_ would be fruit, hallu,
blindness, restore ability (if I have a unihorn), sleep, monster/object
detection, and any _spare_ potions of paralysis, sickness, confusion,
booze, invisibility, polymorph.

> 
> Other questions:
> 
> When can I use a u. horn to recover lost stats? Does it have to be in
> the turn after losing them? I'm asking because sometimes I may need to
> run away from a monster in order not to be hit again while (a) it!

With the exception of a mind flayer brain suck attack (where you could
die) you can restore lost stats later when you're in a safe place.

> Is it important to bless my horn? I'll do it eventually but I'd like
> to know if it's a priority.

I find it helpful later, but it's no high priority in the early game.

> Do I exercise daggers skill by throwing them? I've been doing it for a
> while and I got nothing, the minute I wielded one and used it I got an
> enhancement...

You exercise it when throwing or stabbing, if your character class can
enhance that skill.

> I got an uncursed scroll of genocide... being a Val, is there anything
> particularly nasty to save it for? If I have a hard monster hitting me
> is that a good moment to read it and kill him?

In the early game I'd save it especially for soldier ants (in case you
can not yet handle them).

> At this point (Lvl 11,
> HP=112) shall I consider going to Sokoban and nurse dancing?

Not in my book. But I cannot really comment about that since I don't do
that. Though take care that you won't be surprised by tough monsters.

